  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved 0.485 accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, resnet50) was much weaker at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have no information on whether multiprofile + aggregation improves upon singleprofile for RNA. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly extends the best-performing config by adding multiprofile with simple average-pool aggregation, isolating the effect of profile aggregation on the RNA modality. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a minimal, single-decision change from the current best (profile setting + its required aggregation), so the result cleanly tells us whether multiprofile is worth pursuing across all RNA encoders and fusion strategies. If it helps, it validates a large branch of the search space; if it does not, we can focus budget on encoder and fusion choices within singleprofile. This reduces the most impactful architectural uncertainty before investing in more complex multimodal or learned-encoder experiments."
}

